title: 'Auth: a login answered 2xx without access_token is cached as a token'
updated: 2026-10-06T19:18:57Z
---

`lib/WWW/Keycloak/Auth.pm:185-198` `_grant` takes `$data->{access_token}` without checking it. `read_response` returns `data => undef` for a 2xx whose body is not JSON (a proxy's HTML page, a captive portal), so `_access` becomes undef and `_access_expires` is set 60 s ahead. `token` then returns undef, `Admin::call` (`Admin.pm:111-116`) sends the request without an `Authorization` header (`build_request` skips an undefined bearer), gets a 401, invalidates, logs in again with the same result and finally throws the 401 of the *Admin API* - the caller is told the token was refused, when in fact no token was ever issued.

Same code in the twin: `p5-net-async-keycloak/lib/Net/Async/Keycloak/Auth.pm:170-184`.

Done: `_grant` / `_grant_f` throw `Error::API` (`admin login failed: the token endpoint answered <status> without an access_token`) when `access_token` is missing or empty; a test in `t/` feeds a 200 with an HTML body.

